BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:49957cedffb1823e8ad7097e
SUMMARY:2026-27 CMT Studio Series
DTSTAMP:20260905T080357Z
DTSTART:20260912T233000Z
DTEND:20260912T233000Z
DESCRIPTION:English Lit September 4 - 12\, 2026 English Lit is an original 
	musical comedy that takes audiences on a “CliffsNotes journey” through a v
	ast selection of classic literary works by means of the Broadway musicals 
	they inspired. Humor\, drama\, soaring ballads\, and musical theatre gems 
	will move you... from the page to the stage. Hold on tight\; there will be
	 a test at the end!! (Literally!) In Harmony January 29 - Febuary 6\, 2027
	 In Harmony is a musical journey where life and song blend seamlessly. Thi
	s Studio Series event celebrates musical theatre favorites from every era\
	, chosen to highlight how harmony is something we create together. After a
	ll\, true harmony only emerges when voices unite. In Life. In Song. In Har
	mony. Experience the beauty of making music—and life—together. It's a Smal
	l World March 19 - 27\, 2027 Prepare to "step in time" to the music of the
	 Sherman Brothers! The beloved songs of Mary Poppins\, The Jungle Book\, a
	nd many more come to life as we celebrate the whimsy of childhood\, for th
	e young and old alike.\n\nhttps://www.cincinnatiarts.org/events/detail/cmt
	-studio-series-27
URL:https://www.cincinnatiarts.org/events/detail/cmt-studio-series-27
LOCATION:Fifth Third Bank Theater\, Aronoff Center
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CATEGORIES:Theater
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:d149d8479cf176a243bfe3c6
SUMMARY:Cincinnati Playwrights Initiative: 2026/2027 New Voices Series
DTSTAMP:20260905T080357Z
DTSTART:20260915T230000Z
DTEND:20260915T230000Z
DESCRIPTION:a { text-decoration: none\; color: #464feb\; } tr th\, tr td { 
	border: 1px solid #e6e6e6\; } tr th { background-color: #f5f5f5\; } Cincin
	nati Playwrights Initiative’s New Voices Series returns with a vibrant\, t
	hought‑provoking season of new works! Five staged readings for just $45! T
	his year’s lineup explores resilience\, life-changing choices\, family mys
	teries\, unexpected connections\, and moral dilemmas that ripple across re
	lationships and ambitions. From heartfelt humor to gripping introspection\
	, each play offers fresh perspectives on hope\, identity\, and what might 
	have been. Don’t miss this dynamic celebration of bold storytelling and em
	erging voices! a { text-decoration: none\; color: #464feb\; } tr th\, tr t
	d { border: 1px solid #e6e6e6\; } tr th { background-color: #f5f5f5\; } a 
	{ text-decoration: none\; color: #464feb\; } tr th\, tr td { border: 1px s
	olid #e6e6e6\; } tr th { background-color: #f5f5f5\; } Following each perf
	ormance\, we invite you to stay for live audience talkbacks\, offering the
	 opportunity to share feedback and directly support the playwrights as the
	y continue developing their scripts. The Opposite of Failure: A Full-Lengt
	h Play by Nancy Robinson Crist Tuesday\, September 15\, 2026 a { text-deco
	ration: none\; color: #464feb\; } tr th\, tr td { border: 1px solid #e6e6e
	6\; } tr th { background-color: #f5f5f5\; } Martie has struggled to rebuil
	d her life after her thirty-year marriage ended\, facing chronic depressio
	n and unsuccessful treatments. Just as she begins to lose hope\, an unexpe
	cted circle of people helps her realize that healing means both helping he
	rself and accepting support from others. What Might Have Been: A Full-Leng
	th Drama by Leo Bradley Tuesday\, October 20\, 2026 What Might Have Been f
	ollows the trials and tribulations\, successes and failures\, happiness an
	d sadness\, of two men\, one who follows a safe and conventional life and 
	one who takes a riskier\, more unconventional one. An Evening of One Acts:
	 by Paul Bergman & Jon Singer Tuesday\, November 17\, 20\n\nhttps://www.ci
	ncinnatiarts.org/events/detail/cincinnati-playwrights-initiative-2026-2027
	-new-voices-series
URL:https://www.cincinnatiarts.org/events/detail/cincinnati-playwrights-ini
	tiative-2026-2027-new-voices-series
LOCATION:Fifth Third Bank Theater\, Aronoff Center
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CATEGORIES:Theater
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:4d9ce664a96cda9ce3672d08
SUMMARY:CPI - The Opposite of Failure 
DTSTAMP:20260905T080357Z
DTSTART:20260915T233000Z
DESCRIPTION:The Opposite of Failure: A Full-Length Play by Nancy Robinson C
	rist Synopsis: Martie has been trying to get back on her feet ever since h
	er thirty-year marriage ended. Crippled by chronic depression\, she has tr
	ied - without success - to find a treatment that works. But just when she 
	thinks her life won’t get better\, hope arrives in the form of a philosoph
	ical teen\, a flaky coworker\, an innovative doctor\, and a “flustrated” n
	ephew. Martie learns that\, while it’s important for her to help herself\,
	 it’s just as important to accept help from the other people sharing her c
	orner of the world. Playwright Bio: Nancy Robinson Crist’s first play\, Ev
	erything’s Relative\, was published by Dramatic Publishing in 1990. Over t
	he next eight years she wrote The Case of the Disappearing Drumsticks\, a 
	children’s play\; Murder in Mayberry\, a comedy\; Soul Survivors\, a comed
	y-drama that received a staged reading at Lincoln Center and productions i
	n Chicago and New York\; and Jack the Chipper\, a musical written with com
	poser Mark Hollmann and produced in Chicago. She was hijacked by life for 
	twenty-eight years before returning to her passion in 2026\, writing The O
	pposite of Failure. She lives in Greendale\, Indiana\, with her cat and co
	nfidante\, Javy.\n\nhttps://www.cincinnatiarts.org/events/detail/cpi-the-o
	pposite-of-failure
URL:https://www.cincinnatiarts.org/events/detail/cpi-the-opposite-of-failur
	e
LOCATION:Fifth Third Bank Theater\, Aronoff Center
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CATEGORIES:Theater
DURATION:PT2H
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:c88923322588f379e6f057c1
SUMMARY:The Great Gatsby
DTSTAMP:20260905T080357Z
DTSTART:20260915T233000Z
DESCRIPTION:The party's roaring in Cincinnati! The Great Gatsby is a “Broad
	way extravaganza that explodes with life and energy” (Entertainment Weekly
	). Based on the classic American novel by F. Scott Fitzgerald\, the Tony A
	ward®-winning new musical is an unforgettable journey of love\, wealth and
	 tragedy that brings the Roaring Twenties to life on stage. Directed by Ma
	rc Bruni (Beautiful: The Carole King Musical)\, this story of extravagance
	 and longing features choreography by Dominique Kelley (So You Think You C
	an Dance)\, a book by Kait Kerrigan (The Mad Ones) and a jazz- and pop-inf
	luenced original score by Jason Howland (Little Women) and Nathan Tysen (P
	aradise Square).\n\nhttps://www.cincinnatiarts.org/events/detail/the-great
	-gatsby
URL:https://www.cincinnatiarts.org/events/detail/the-great-gatsby
LOCATION:Procter & Gamble Hall\, Aronoff Center
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CATEGORIES:Theater
DURATION:PT2H
END:VEVENT
